{"seconds": 35.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! **Rd4+** is clearly the best move. It forces White into a bad position where Black wins material in all variations. The key idea is that the rook check on d4 is a **fork** (or discovered attack setup), and regardless of White's response, Black wins.\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nWhen your opponent's king is exposed and your rook can give check, look for forcing sequences. Here, **Rd4+** is a rook fork that attacks both the king on g4 and the rook on d1. In every line\u2014whether White blocks with Be4, moves the king, or recaptures\u2014Black wins material. The lesson: checks that fork multiple pieces often win material without requiring tactics to remember.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rd4+\", \"line\": [\"Rd4+\", \"Be4\", \"Rxe4+\", \"Rxe4\", \"Qxa2\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "square": "h2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "square": "d8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "square": "g6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "move": "Rd4+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r2k1/p5p1/2p2pBp/4B3/2P3K1/6P1/P6q/3RR3 b - - 1 26", "move": "Qe2+"}}, {"tool": "che